  "problem": "For the function $f(x,y),$ calculate $\\frac{{\u2202}^{2}f}{\u2202{y}^{2}}$ given that $\\frac{\u2202f}{\u2202y}=\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{{x}^{3}+{y}^{3}}.$",
  "worked_solution": "To find $\\frac{{\u2202}^{2}f}{\u2202{y}^{2}}$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative $\\frac{\u2202f}{\u2202y}$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\u2202}^{2}f}{\u2202{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(\\frac{\u2202f}{\u2202y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{{x}^{3}+{y}^{3}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{6y({x}^{3}+{y}^{3})-3{y}^{2}(3{y}^{2})}{{({x}^{3}+{y}^{3})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6y{x}^{3}+6{y}^{4}-9{y}^{4}}{{({x}^{3}+{y}^{3})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6y{x}^{3}-3{y}^{4}}{{({x}^{3}+{y}^{3})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3y(2{x}^{3}-{y}^{3})}{{({x}^{3}+{y}^{3})}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
